    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Whathave cupcakesgotto dowithcups, asksonereader"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 48,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 495.805, 525.498, 523.527, 531.529 ],
    "font" : "StRyde-Light",
    "font size" : 5.244,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "AFP/GETTY"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 26,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 297.126, 425.554, 364.884, 511.194 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "was more common than in England. She was palbably relieved when I explained they meant “what’s this”and “where’s that”, thereby easing her mind that she had not married into a culture of coarse swearers! JIMWOOD OTTERY ST MARY, DEVON"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H5",
    "id" : 27,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 297.125, 399.695, 361.318, 419.222 ],
    "heading level" : 5,
    "font" : "Stag-Bold",
    "font size" : 8.99,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Goodcleanfun onthebeach"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 28,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 297.125, 276.124, 366.842, 397.361 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "It’s not just the Australians who can celebrate without leaving masses of litter. On holiday in the South of France last summer, we were among thousands who ﬁlled the beach and streets at Valras-Plage to watch a spectacular ﬁrework display celebrating le 14 Juillet. When everyone left, the beach was spotless! LYNNEPEMBERTON ABBOTS MORTON, WORCESTERSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 31,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 375.632, 468.306, 436.904, 511.228 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "The accident is caused by others’ impatience, inattention, or loss of control. MFOSTER SHROPSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H5",
    "id" : 32,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 375.634, 442.4, 437.663, 461.927 ],
    "heading level" : 5,
    "font" : "Stag-Bold",
    "font size" : 8.99,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Settersgetting sneakier"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 33,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 375.634, 318.829, 444.041, 440.066 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "I have been a moderately successful tackler of cryptic crosswords for many years, but I am ﬁnding them increasingly challenging. Occasionally, even after seeing the solution, I still don’t get it. Is this a sign that my 87-year-old brain is not quite up to the job or are the setters simply becoming more and more sneaky? GEOFFIVORY FRINTON-ON-SEA, ESSEX"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H5",
    "id" : 34,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 375.634, 292.934, 437.697, 312.461 ],
    "heading level" : 5,
    "font" : "Stag-Bold",
    "font size" : 8.99,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "No-showGP chargesunfair"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 35,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 375.634, 276.157, 440.861, 290.6 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Concerned about people missing doctors’"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 36,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 454.632, 461.198, 524.171, 511.239 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "appointments, Stuart Ackland suggests (Your View, 3 January) that patients have to make an advance credit\\debit card “booking”, with a charge deducted for a no-show."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 37,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 454.632, 347.284, 524.133, 461.402 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "But what about people like me who don’t have any such cards? With my GP practice, it is hard to get through on the telephone to make an appointment, and I regularly hang up after being kept on hold for ages. Might people similarly be calling to make a cancellation but are unable to get a response? TIMMICKLEBURGH GRIMSBY, NORTH LINCOLNSHIRE"
  }, {
    "type" : "heading",
    "pdfua_tag" : "H5",
    "id" : 38,
    "level" : "Subtitle",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 454.63, 321.404, 522.924, 340.931 ],
    "heading level" : 5,
    "font" : "Stag-Bold",
    "font size" : 8.99,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "Unfaircertainly butnotracist"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 39,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 454.63, 276.149, 515.884, 319.07 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "I completely agree with Deborah Orr (My View, 3 January) that the imposition of repatriation costs on women escaping from"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 40,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 533.379, 617.758, 601.306, 703.398 ],
    "font" : "StRydeRegular",
    "font size" : 6.368,
    "text color" : "[0.13725490868091583, 0.12156862765550613, 0.125490203499794]",
    "content" : "forced marriages abroad is unworthy of our government. However, I feel that her charge of racism on the part of the Foreign Ofﬁce is unfounded. I am sure that any white British woman repatriated in similar circumstances would be presented with the same bill."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 41,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 533.379, 603.519, 589.106, 617.962 ],
